    "lawCode": "Amd §292, Exec L",
    "lawSection": "Executive Law",
    "memo": "\n \nBILL NUMBER: S4211\n\nSPONSOR: SEPULVEDA\n \nTITLE OF BILL:  An act to amend the executive law, in relation to\namending the definition of pregnancy-related condition\n\n \nPURPOSE OR GENERAL IDEA OF BILL:\n\nThe purpose of this bill is to clarify that \"lactation\" is protected in\nthe workplace.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nSection one of the bill would amend the definition of \"pregnancy related\ncondition\" within the Human Rights Law to include lactation.\n\nSection two of the bill is the effective date.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nBreastfeeding parents should be guaranteed the right to use break time\nto provide breast milk for their newborn children at work and the right\nto reasonable efforts by an employer to provide a private space to do\nso. This bill would ensure employers are following the Human Rights Law\nby clarifying that lactation is a pregnancy-related condition requiring\nemployers to make reasonable accommodations in the workplace.\n\n \nPRIOR LEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nNew Bill\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS FOR STATE AND LOCAL GOVERNMENTS:\n\nMinimal\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nImmediate\n",
